{
  "input": "Supervised aur unsupervised learning ke beech do antar bataiye.",
  "output_1": "1. Supervision: Reinforcement learning mein ek reward signal se seekhna shamil hai, jahan ek agent ek environment ke saath interact karta hai aur rewards ya penalties ke roop mein feedback prapt karta hai. Agent samay ke saath apne cumulative reward ko maximize karna seekhta hai. Doosri taraf, unsupervised learning mein koi spasht supervision ya feedback shamil nahi hota hai. Yeh bina kisi vishisht lakshya ya reward signal ke unlabeled data mein patterns ya structures ko khojne par focus karta hai.\n\n2. Goal-oriented vs. Goal-agnostic: Reinforcement learning goal-oriented hai, jahan agent ek vishisht reward signal ko maximize karne ke liye actions lena seekhta hai. Agent sakriya roop se environment ko explore karta hai, apne actions se seekhta hai, aur vanchhit lakshya ko prapt karne ke liye apne vyavahar ko uske anusaar adjust karta hai. Iske vipreet, unsupervised learning goal-agnostic hai. Iska uddeshya bina kisi purv-paribhashit uddeshya ya lakshya ke data mein nihit patterns ya structures ko khojna hai. Focus aisi representations ya features ko seekhne par hai jo data ke mool structure ko capture karte hain.",
  "output_2": "Supervised aur unsupervised learning ke beech do mukhya antar yeh hain ki supervised learning ke liye labeled data ki zaroorat hoti hai jabki unsupervised learning ke liye nahi, aur supervised learning bhavishya ke parinaam ki bhavishyavani karne ke liye data ki matra ka upyog karta hai jabki unsupervised learning kisi vishisht parinaam ki bhavishyavani kiye bina ek dataset ke bheetar patterns ya sambandhon ko khojta hai."
}

