{
  "input": "Shakespearean aur modern English ke beech ke differences ko ek brief example ke saath describe karo.",
  "output_1": "Shakespearean English aur modern English, language ke do alag forms hain. Dono ke beech major differences pronunciation, grammar, aur vocabulary mein hain. Shakespearean English ka pronunciation modern English ke pronunciation se alag hai, kyunki yeh Old English se zyada heavily influenced hai. Modern English ki grammar Shakespearean English se zyada simplified ho gayi hai, jismein ek zyada complex grammar structure use hota tha. Iske alawa, Shakespearean English ki vocabulary modern English se badi thi, kyunki isne Latin, Italian, aur French jaise kai languages se words borrow kiye the.",
  "output_2": "Shakespearean English, jise Early Modern English bhi kehte hain, late 15th se late 17th century ke dauraan use ki jaati thi aur iski pehchan iski unique vocabulary, grammar, aur pronunciation se hoti hai. Ismein aksar aise words use hote hain jo aajkal common use mein nahi hain, aur iska sentence structure zyada complex ho sakta hai. Wahin doosri taraf, Modern English, English language ka woh form hai jo late 17th century se ab tak use hota hai. Iske sentence structures simpler hain aur yeh ek zyada standardized grammar aur spelling use karta hai. Vocabulary bhi alag hai, jismein kai words time ke saath evolve hue hain ya unka meaning change ho gaya hai.\nExample ke liye, Shakespearean English mein, koi sun sakta hai \"But, soft! what light through yonder window breaks? It is the east, and Juliet is the sun.\" (Romeo and Juliet), jabki Modern English mein iska translation aise ho sakta hai: \"But wait, what's that light coming from the window over there? It's Juliet, and she is like the sun.\""
}

