{
  "input": "Collatz conjecture ko solve karne ka possible tareeka",
  "output_1": "Collatz Conjecture mathematics mein ek unsolved problem hai jo positive integers ke liye defined ek particular sequence ke behavior ke baare mein poochta hai. Collatz Conjecture ka ek possible solution ek computer program use karna ho sakta hai taaki required calculations perform kiye ja sakein. Lekin, iske doosre solutions bhi ho sakte hain, aur exact solution sequence aur problem ke details par depend karega.",
  "output_2": "Collatz Conjecture mathematics ka ek famous unsolved problem hai, jise 3n + 1 conjecture ya Ulam conjecture ke naam se bhi jaana jaata hai. Yeh kehta hai ki kisi bhi positive integer n ke liye, agar n even hai, to use 2 se divide karo, warna, agar n odd hai, to use 3 se multiply karke 1 add karo. Phir result ko lo aur is process ko naye value ke saath repeat karte jao, and so on. Conjecture yeh claim karta hai ki aap chahe kisi bhi positive integer se shuru karein, yeh process hamesha aakhir mein number 1 tak pahunch jaayega.\n\nFor example, agar hum number 6 se shuru karte hain, jo even hai, to hum use 2 se divide karke 3 paate hain. Kyunki 3 odd hai, hum use 3 se multiply karke 1 add karte hain to 10 milta hai. Isi tarah continue karne par, humein sequence 6, 3, 10, 5, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1 milta hai. Conjecture yeh assert karta hai ki yeh sequence hamesha 1 par terminate hota hai, chahe aap kisi bhi number se shuru karein.\n\nCollatz Conjecture ki simplicity ke bawajood, yeh abhi bhi unsolved hai, aur koi bhi ise sabhi positive integers ke liye prove ya disprove nahi kar paaya hai. Halaanki ise computer dwara ek incredibly large number of cases ke liye verify kiya ja chuka hai, yeh mathematics ke sabse intriguing open problems mein se ek bana hua hai."
}

