{
  "input": "Supervised aur unsupervised learning ke beech do differences batao.",
  "output_1": "1. Supervision: Reinforcement learning mein ek reward signal se learning hoti hai, jahan ek agent environment ke saath interact karta hai aur rewards ya penalties ke form mein feedback receive karta hai. Agent time ke saath apne cumulative reward ko maximize karna seekhta hai. Doosri taraf, unsupervised learning mein koi explicit supervision ya feedback nahi hota. Iska focus unlabeled data mein patterns ya structures find karne par hota hai, bina kisi specific goal ya reward signal ke.\n\n2. Goal-oriented vs. Goal-agnostic: Reinforcement learning goal-oriented hota hai, jahan agent ek specific reward signal ko maximize karne ke liye actions lena seekhta hai. Agent actively environment ko explore karta hai, apne actions se seekhta hai, aur desired goal achieve karne ke liye apne behavior ko accordingly adjust karta hai. Iske contrast mein, unsupervised learning goal-agnostic hota hai. Iska aim data mein inherent patterns ya structures discover karna hota hai bina kisi predefined objective ya goal ke. Focus aise representations ya features learn karne par hota hai jo data ke underlying structure ko capture karein.",
  "output_2": "Supervised aur unsupervised learning ke beech do main differences yeh hain ki supervised learning ko labeled data chahiye hota hai jabki unsupervised learning ko nahi, aur supervised learning future outcome predict karne ke liye data ki quantity use karta hai jabki unsupervised learning ek dataset ke andar patterns ya relationships find karta hai bina kisi specific outcome ko predict kiye."
}

