{
  "input": "Psychology insaano aur gair-insaano mein mann aur vyavhaar ka adhyayan hai. Psychologists dimaag ke ubharte gunon ki samajh haasil karna chahte hain, is discipline ko neuroscience se jodte hue. Social scientists ke roop mein, psychologists vyaktiyon aur samuhon ke vyavhaar ko samajhna chahte hain. Kya psychology ka koi aisa field hai jo isse deal karta hai ki ek vyakti apne aas-paas ki cheezon aur jagahon par kaise react karta hai, woh kya hai?\nHint: Psychology mein chetan aur achetna ghatnaon ka adhyayan shaamil hai, jismein bhavnaayein aur vichaar bhi shaamil hain. Yeh ek bahut bade scope wala academic discipline hai, jo natural aur social sciences ke beech ki seemaon ko paar karta hai.",
  "output_1": "Haan, yeh Environmental Psychology hai.",
  "output_2": "Haan, psychology ka ek field hai jo isse deal karta hai ki ek vyakti apne aas-paas ki cheezon aur jagahon par kaise react karta hai. Ise \"Psychology\" kehte hain. Yeh jaanchta hai ki log apne physical environment ko kaise samajhte hain aur uske saath kaise interact karte hain, jismein unke ghar, kaam karne ki jagah, aur public spaces shaamil hain. Yeh explore karta hai ki lighting, temperature, shor, aur layout jaise environmental factors insaani vyavhaar, mood, aur kalyaan ko kaise prabhavit kar sakte hain. Yeh urban planning, sustainability, aur swasthya aur kalyaan ko badhava dene ke liye public spaces ke design jaise vishayon ka bhi adhyayan kar sakta hai."
}

{
  "input": "Neeche describe ki gayi situation par apni best advice dijiye.\n\nBete ko peanut allergy hai, aur school usse lagatar peanuts deta rehta hai ya lene deta hai. Yeh school ke second day se hi ek ongoing issue raha hai jab usse peanut butter crackers diye gaye the. Humne isse ek tarah se brush off kar diya ki naya school year hai, naye students hain, teachers first graders se deal karte hue thode frazzled hain, koi real big deal nahi hai. Uski allergy itni severe nahi hai par phir bhi isse deal karna fun nahi hai aur potentially life-threatening ho sakti hai. Humne saal shuru hone se pehle hi school ko uski allergy ke baare mein inform kar diya tha aur teacher se directly baat bhi ki thi kyunki agar koi aur parent snack na laaye toh din ka default snack peanut butter crackers hi hota hai. Humne uske liye ek special alternative purchase karne ka offer bhi diya, par unhone kaha ki yeh unnecessary hai kyunki unke paas doosre alternatives hain. Toh humne socha ki issue over ho gaya hai jab kuch weeks baad yeh phir se hua, is baar unhone claim kiya ki usne doosre student ka snack grab kar liya aur unke rokne se pehle hi bhaag kar kha liya. Ab mera chhota beta thoda sa hardhead ho sakta hai aur main potentially aisa hote hue dekh sakti hoon isliye humne usse phir se peanuts aur woh uske liye kitne dangerous hain, is baare mein baat ki. Woh lagatar adamantly deny karta raha ki usne aisa kiya aur bola ki Mrs ne usse woh diye the. Phir humne decide kiya ki principal ke saath ek meeting karni chahiye, teacher ko blame karne ya uspar jhoot bolne ka accuse karne ke liye nahi, balki hopefully is cheez ko control mein laane ke liye. Phir se kuch weeks tak koi issue nahi hua, phir yeh dobara ho gaya. Ek baar phir story yeh hai ki \"he grabbed it and ran off and ate the whole package before we caught him\". Okay, toh ek 6-saal ka bachcha crackers ka ek unopened package grab karne mein, ek teacher aur ek aide ko elude karne mein aur pakde jaane se pehle poora package khaane mein manage kar gaya? Woh ro raha hai aur humse swear kar raha hai ki usse woh diye gaye the, aur itne saare incidents ke baad humein uski baat par believe karna hi padega. Principal aur teacher ke saath ek aur meeting se humein yeh jawab mila \"Do not worry! This won't happen again\". Humne apne bete ke saath ek aur lamba sit down kiya yeh explain karne ke liye ki agar tumhe kuch diya bhi jaaye, toh pooch lo ki usmein peanuts ya doosre nuts toh nahi hain. Phir, the very next school day (meeting Friday ko hui thi) usse phir se peanut butter crackers ka snack diya gaya lekin is baar usne pucha ki kya ismein nuts hain aur tab usse alternative diya gaya. Humein laga ki yeh kind of sucks ki bachche ko yahan adult banna pad raha hai lekin at the end of the day, woh nuts ke baare mein puchna seekh raha hai. Humne principal ko ek email bheja jismein issue ko detail mein bataya aur kaha ki agar usse dobara peanuts diye gaye toh humara next stop school board hoga. Humein response mila \"If he's asking now what's the problem? He should have known to ask to begin with. We are teachers, not parents.\" Kuch time tak humein koi issue nahi hua, is hafte tak. Kuch parents snack time ke liye PB&J sandwiches laaye aur usse ek de diya gaya. Woh nuts ke baare mein puchna bhool gaya par socha \"It was only in the crackers\". Humein pata chala ki parent ko class mein nut allergy ke baare mein aware tha (yeh parent snack sheet par hai) aur woh ek sirf jelly wala sandwich laaye the jo peanut butter walon se separate banaya gaya tha. Usse yeh wala nahi diya gaya. Humne ek din hospital mein spend kiya. Humne usse nuts ke baare mein endless talks ki hain aur usse teach karne ki poori koshish karte hain lekin kuch blame toh yahan teachers par bhi aana chahiye na? Kya schools ki allergies se deal karne ki koi obligation nahi hoti? School lunch mein isse zero issues lagte hain aur unhone usse kabhi koi nut nahi diya jabki menu rotation mein kai cheezein hain jinmein nuts hote hain. Usse ek special tray milti hai jo kisi bhi nut ke aas paas nahi thi. Yeh Indiana mein hai, koi bhi help appreciate ki jaayegi.",
  "output_1": "In logon par bilkul bhi trust nahi kiya ja sakta, aapko uske school mein ek scene create karna chahiye taaki logon ko unke ill behavior ke consequences dikhein.",
  "output_2": "Kya hospital visit se aapke koi costs lage? Ho sakta hai school ko apne actions mein problem na dikhe, lekin unke insurance ko dikh sakti hai. Shayad ek claim submit karne se unka attention mil jaaye?"
}

