  "output_1": "1. Supervision: Reinforcement learning mein ek reward signal se learning hoti hai, jahan ek agent environment ke saath interact karta hai aur use rewards ya penalties ke form mein feedback milta hai. Agent time ke saath apne cumulative reward ko maximize karna seekhta hai. Doosri taraf, unsupervised learning mein koi bhi explicit supervision ya feedback involve nahi hota. Iska focus unlabeled data mein patterns ya structures find karne par hota hai, bina kisi specific goal ya reward signal ke.\n\n2. Goal-oriented vs. Goal-agnostic: Reinforcement learning goal-oriented hai, jahan agent aise actions lena seekhta hai jo ek specific reward signal ko maximize karte hain. Agent actively environment ko explore karta hai, apne actions se seekhta hai, aur desired goal achieve karne ke liye apne behavior ko accordingly adjust karta hai. Iske contrast mein, unsupervised learning goal-agnostic hai. Iska aim data mein inherent patterns ya structures ko discover karna hota hai, bina kisi predefined objective ya goal ke. Focus aise representations ya features learn karne par hota hai jo data ke underlying structure ko capture karte hain.",
